<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tunja</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tunja is the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boyaca-department">Boyacá</a> in the Eastern Andes of Colombia. Founded by the Spanish in 1539 on the site of Hunza, the seat of the Muisca zaque, it became one of the main towns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>. During the independence period it was the seat of the congress of the United Provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tunja.jpg" alt="Tunja" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edisonalv · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CatedralTunja1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
